#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/adjust-the-double-click-speed.md:0
msgid ""
"Change how quickly you must press the mouse button twice to double-click on "
"Ubuntu Desktop, and check for a faulty mouse."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/adjust-the-double-click-speed.md:7
msgid "Topics: Accessibility Customization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/adjust-the-double-click-speed.md:11
msgid "Adjust the double-click speed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/adjust-the-double-click-speed.md:13
msgid ""
"Double-clicking only happens when you press the mouse button twice quickly "
"enough. If the second press is too long after the first, you’ll just get two "
"separate clicks, not a double click. If you have difficulty pressing the "
"mouse button quickly, you should increase the timeout."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/adjust-the-double-click-speed.md:15
msgid "Open the Activities overview and start typing **accessibility**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/adjust-the-double-click-speed.md:16
msgid "Click {guilabel}`Accessibility` to open the panel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/adjust-the-double-click-speed.md:17
msgid "Open the {guilabel}`Pointing & Clicking` section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/adjust-the-double-click-speed.md:18
msgid ""
"Adjust the {guilabel}`Double-Click Delay` slider to a value you find "
"comfortable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/adjust-the-double-click-speed.md:20
msgid ""
"If your mouse double-clicks when you want it to single-click even though you "
"have increased the double-click timeout, your mouse may be faulty. Try "
"plugging a different mouse into your computer and see if that works "
"properly. Alternatively, plug your mouse into a different computer and see "
"if it still has the same problem."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/adjust-the-double-click-speed.md:23
msgid ""
"This setting will affect both your mouse and touchpad, as well as any other "
"pointing device."
msgstr ""
